WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.275
The change makes finish_walkthrough warn when Chromium is

2
00:00:03.275 --> 00:00:04.120
missing.

3
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.545
It is mostly right,

4
00:00:05.545 --> 00:00:07.575
but one fix probably won't work for the

5
00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:09.550
user who follows it.

6
00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:11.708
The core change is correct.

7
00:00:11.708 --> 00:00:14.158
A missing browser now raises a warning,

8
00:00:14.158 --> 00:00:16.570
no_browser, instead of an info line,

9
00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.625
and the tests cover it.

10
00:00:18.745 --> 00:00:20.675
But the fix it tells users to follow

11
00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:22.107
can silently fail.

12
00:00:22.107 --> 00:00:23.795
That is the one should-fix.

13
00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:25.775
The rest is minor.

14
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.870
_check_layout used to return one string.

15
00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.182
Now it returns a code and a reason,

16
00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:33.425
so a missing browser and a failed drawing

17
00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:35.250
can be told apart.

18
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.582
The timeout stays an info finding.

19
00:00:37.582 --> 00:00:39.008
That split is right:

20
00:00:39.008 --> 00:00:41.400
a missing install is the user's to fix,

21
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.375
a timeout is not.

22
00:00:43.495 --> 00:00:45.695
The log line fires once per daemon,

23
00:00:45.695 --> 00:00:47.145
so it can't flood.

24
00:00:47.145 --> 00:00:49.187
I also checked that None still means the

25
00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:52.400
check was off, so SHOWNTELL_FINISH_CHECK=0

26
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.075
stays quiet.

27
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.125
Suspected from reading the code,

28
00:00:56.125 --> 00:00:57.170
not run.

29
00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.450
The build check](#L3 "lock.get("version")") compares the version and a

30
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.025
hash of showntell's own files.

31
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.988
So a running base-install daemon counts as current

32
00:01:04.988 --> 00:01:06.295
and is reused.

33
00:01:06.295 --> 00:01:08.045
It never imported Playwright,

34
00:01:08.045 --> 00:01:10.775
so finish still says no_browser.

35
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.870
Name showntell stop in the hint,

36
00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:15.975
or have ensure check whether Playwright imports.

37
00:01:16.095 --> 00:01:18.000
The author may say a fresh machine has

38
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:18.995
no daemon.

39
00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:22.425
True, but this warning appears mid-session.

40
00:01:22.845 --> 00:01:25.157
The old hint was written for export.

41
00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:27.395
The new one reuses the doctor text,

42
00:01:27.395 --> 00:01:30.750
which tells you to start showntell mcp.

43
00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:34.075
So showntell export --mp4 without

44
00:01:34.075 --> 00:01:36.712
Playwright now prints a command for the MCP

45
00:01:36.712 --> 00:01:37.632
server.

46
00:01:37.632 --> 00:01:40.558
The install and Chromium steps still apply,

47
00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:43.425
so it's confusing rather than wrong.

48
00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.882
Also, capture now imports doctor for a string.

49
00:01:46.882 --> 00:01:48.800
Move the constants somewhere neutral,

50
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.625
like config, so the dependency points one way.

51
00:01:53.095 --> 00:01:54.545
Four small things.

52
00:01:54.545 --> 00:01:56.600
The version pin is the one most likely

53
00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.537
to bite: the next release leaves stale commands

54
00:01:59.537 --> 00:02:01.075
in the README.

55
00:02:01.195 --> 00:02:03.495
The missing commands cost the user a step;

56
00:02:03.495 --> 00:02:05.650
the message could carry them.

57
00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.800
The test gaps and the global flag go

58
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.720
together: add a fixture that resets the flag,

59
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.300
then test the log-once path.

60
00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.250
The change does what it says,

61
00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.520
and the tests pass for what they cover.

62
00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.300
The stale daemon comes first,

63
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.245
because it decides whether the warning leads anywhere.

64
00:02:22.245 --> 00:02:24.725
The export hint is next.

65
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.225
The rest are small clean-ups that can follow

66
00:02:27.225 --> 00:02:28.950
in another commit.
